[?2004l[?2004h> Each page is applied in sequence-number order, including tombstones, and committed
[?2004l[?2004h> atomically with its `next_cursor`. Empty sequence windows do not end the sync:
[?2004l[?2004h> only `has_more = false` does. If a request or page fails, the next run resumes at
[?2004l[?2004h> the last committed page. A run with no new changes makes one request from the
[?2004l[?2004h> saved cursor. Invalid/expired-epoch cursors are reported as errors, not silently
